<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/12th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Rignano</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1137">1137</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Rignano was fought on 30 October 1137 near Rignano Garganico in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/apulia">Apulia</a> between King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roger-ii-of-sicily">Roger II of Sicily</a> and the rebel Ranulf of Alife, supported by troops left behind by Emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lothair-i">Lothair</a> III. Roger was defeated, and Duke <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sergius-vii-of-naples">Sergius VII of Naples</a>, who had submitted to him and fought on his side, was killed. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/naples">Naples</a> then passed under Roger's direct rule.</p></div>
